## Why This Is Asked
Examines ability to tame CPU scheduling and memory reclaim in multi-tenant Linux deployments under bursty workloads.

## Key Concepts
- cgroup v2 cpu.max and CPU weight for per-tenant QoS
- cpuset and CPU affinity to confine tenants
- memory reclaim behavior and swappiness tuning
- BPF-based observability for per-tenant latency, IRQs, cache misses
- phased testing, safe rollback, and controlled rollouts

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lightweight latency probe template (pseudo)
async function measureLatency(endpoint){
  const t0 = performance.now();
  await fetch(endpoint);
  return performance.now() - t0;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify safe rollback criteria during staged tests?
- Which metrics dashboards and alerts would you configure for sustained SLOs?

## Why This Is Asked
Real-world WAL tail latency can throttle throughput in bursts; this question probes capability to diagnose IO path bottlenecks and apply production-grade mitigations that don’t compromise data integrity.

## Key Concepts
- IO scheduling and blk-mq
- Per-disk and per-tenant I/O control (cgroups v2)
- CPU/IRQ affinity and NUMA awareness
- WAL isolation strategies and PostgreSQL tuning
- Rigorous load-testing and safe rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js: simple iostat collector for WAL latency analysis
const {spawn} = require('child_process');
const log = require('fs').createWriteStream('/var/log/iostat_wal.log', {flags:'a'});
const proc = spawn('iostat', ['-x','1']);
proc.stdout.on('data', data => log.write(data));
proc.stderr.on('data', d => process.stderr.write(d));
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify data durability isn’t compromised during rollback?
- Which metrics/logs would you baseline before and after changes, and how would you automate rollback if thresholds are not met?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests Linux networking, virtualization concepts, and QoS under multi-tenant load in a real-world VPN gateway.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant namespaces/VRF routing
- XDP/BPF for ACLs and QoS
- tc/qdisc HTB or fq_codel per tenant
- IRQ affinity and CPU pinning
- NUMA awareness and tenant cgroups
- Observability with iperf/netperf

## Code Example

```javascript
// High-level pseudo steps (not executed as-is)
const tenants = ["t1","t2"];
for (const t of tenants) {
  const ns = createNamespace(`vn_${t}`);
  setupVRF(ns, t);
  bindVpnWorkerToNamespace(ns);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would tail latency be measured and bounded at 99th percentile?
- How to safely onboard/offboard tenants without disruption?
